---
import ServicePage from "../../components/ServicePage.astro";

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "What is the difference between trimming and pruning?",
    a: `Trimming mostly keeps a tree neat and clear of the house, roof, lines or walkways. Pruning is done for the tree's health and structure: removing dead, diseased or weak limbs. Many jobs combine both, and an estimate should say which limbs are involved.`,
  },
  {
    q: "How often should trees be trimmed in South Florida?",
    a: `Fast-growing trees often need attention every year or two, and many people have trees checked before hurricane season. Palms are usually trimmed when fronds die or hang over a roof, pool or walkway.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Can palm trees be trimmed or removed near a pool?",
    a: `Yes, tall palms near pools, houses and pavers are common jobs. The crown has to be lowered carefully, so mention the pool and any screens or pavers in your request.`,
  },
  {
    q: "What does stump grinding involve?",
    a: `A grinder cuts the stump below ground level so you can lay sod or plant again. Ask for it to be quoted together with a removal; it is usually cheaper than a separate visit.`,
  },
  {
    q: "Who does the work?",
    a: `Independent tree care professionals, matched to your request. SF Tree Removal is an online service that passes your request on; we do not perform the work. You agree the scope and price directly with the professional.`,
  },
];
const extras = [
  {
    "topper": "Choose a service",
    "title": "Which Service Do You Need?",
    "image": "aerial-lift",
    "html": "<ul><li><strong><a href=\"/tree-removal/\">Tree removal</a></strong> for dead, leaning, damaged or unwanted trees.</li><li><strong><a href=\"/emergency-tree-removal/\">Emergency tree removal</a></strong> for a tree on a house, car or driveway, or near power lines.</li><li><strong><a href=\"/tree-trimming/\">Tree trimming and pruning</a></strong> to keep trees healthy, strong and clear of the house.</li><li><strong><a href=\"/stump-grinding/\">Stump grinding</a></strong> after a removal or for an old stump.</li><li><strong><a href=\"/certified-arborist/\">Arborist assessments</a></strong> when you are not sure what a tree needs, or need documentation.</li></ul>"
  },
  {
    "topper": "Through the year",
    "title": "Tree Care Through the South Florida Year",
    "image": "beach-palms",
    "html": "<p>There is no true off-season for trees here, but there is a rhythm. Late winter and spring are good for assessments and structural pruning. The hurricane season from June 1 to November 30 is when dead wood and weak trees matter most. After any storm, check for damage and cracks, and keep clear of anything near lines.</p><p>See our <a href=\"/tree-care-guides/hurricane-tree-preparation/\">hurricane tree checklist</a> and <a href=\"/tree-care-guides/tree-removal-after-hurricane/\">what to do after a storm</a>.</p>"
  }
];
---

<ServicePage
  title="Tree Services in South Florida | Free Estimates"
  description="All tree services in South Florida in one place: removal, trimming, stump grinding, emergency work and arborist reports. Free local estimates."
  service={{
    name: "Tree Trimming and Stump Grinding Estimates",
    serviceType: "Tree trimming and stump grinding estimate matching",
    description: "Free estimates for tree trimming, pruning, palm work and stump grinding from independent local tree care professionals in South Florida.",
  }}
  badge="TREE SERVICES"
  h1="Tree Services in South Florida"
  lead="Removal, trimming, stump grinding and arborist reports. Pick what you need and get a free estimate from an independent local professional."
  intro={[
    "Regular trimming is the cheapest way to avoid an expensive tree problem. In South Florida, fast growth and storm season mean branches reach roofs, wires and pools quickly.",
    "Send one request through the <a href=\"/contact-us/\">contact form</a> and we connect you with an independent tree care professional for a free estimate. We are active in the Fort Lauderdale area and adding professionals elsewhere; see <a href=\"/areas/#coverage\">where we are active</a>. We don't do the work ourselves, so you can compare and agree every detail directly.",
  ]}
  coversTitle="What You Can Ask For"
  covers={[
    { name: "Tree trimming", note: "Shaping and thinning to keep branches off the roof, walls, wires and walkways, and to let light through." },
    { name: "Pruning for health", note: "Removing dead, diseased or weakly attached limbs before they fall, especially ahead of hurricane season." },
    { name: "Palm trimming", note: "Removing dead fronds, seed pods and coconuts from royal, coconut and other palms near houses and pools." },
    { name: "Stump grinding", note: "Grinding the stump below ground level after a removal so you can lay sod or plant again." },
    { name: "Storm preparation", note: "Reducing the weight and wind sail of large trees before the season. See our hurricane checklist." },
    { name: "Tree assessment", note: "A health and risk check by an arborist when you are unsure whether a tree should be pruned or removed." },
  ]}
  detailTitle="Find the Right Service"
  detail={`<p>Each service has its own page with what it covers and what affects the price: <a href="/tree-removal/">tree removal</a>, <a href="/emergency-tree-removal/">emergency tree removal</a>, <a href="/tree-trimming/">tree trimming and pruning</a>, <a href="/stump-grinding/">stump grinding</a> and <a href="/certified-arborist/">arborist assessments</a>. Not sure what is free? Read <a href="/free-tree-removal/">what is actually free</a>.</p>
<h3>Getting a useful estimate</h3>
<p>The more you tell the professional, the closer the first number will be to the final one. Include:</p>
<ul>
  <li>The type of tree and roughly how tall it is.</li>
  <li>What should be trimmed (limbs over the roof, a lifted canopy, dead fronds) and what the tree is close to.</li>
  <li>Whether you want the stump ground and the wood hauled away.</li>
  <li>Photos, if you can send them.</li>
</ul>
<p>Ask for the scope in writing and for proof of license and insurance before work starts. Trimming that removes too much of a tree can harm it, and some cities regulate pruning of protected trees; read about <a href="/tree-removal-permits/">permits</a> if you are unsure. See also the <a href="/tree-care-guides/hurricane-tree-preparation/">hurricane tree checklist</a>.</p>`}
  faqs={faqs}
  image="canopy-climber"
  introImage="crane-lift"
  introTitle="Everything Tree Care, in One Place"
  extras={extras}
/>
